    <entry xml:lang="en">
        <title>More focus on my projects</title>
        <published>2026-04-02T00:00:00+00:00</published>
        <updated>2026-04-02T00:00:00+00:00</updated>
        
        <author>
          <name>Unknown</name>
        </author>
        
        <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://tmahmood.github.io/blog/2026-apr-02/"/>
        <id>https://tmahmood.github.io/blog/2026-apr-02/</id>
        
        <content type="html" xml:base="https://tmahmood.github.io/blog/2026-apr-02/">&lt;h1 id=&quot;more-focus-on-my-projects&quot;&gt;More focus on my projects&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So, I am putting more focus on my projects last few months. Also learning, blender, pixel art, and sketching. 2026 has not been a good year for me. But I am looking forward to fixing it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;task-warrior-web&quot;&gt;Task warrior web&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Taskwarrior Web came along nicely, all the nitty clippy warnings are gone, more tests, and a lot of bug fixes. Looking forward to getting more features done in coming months.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;journal-app&quot;&gt;Journal app&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Besides, I am working on a journal app, with task management and some other interesting concepts. I am really looking forward to get it up and running soon. Want to make it a product out of it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;rift&quot;&gt;RIFT&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A fast, simple, app launcher. Instead of discovering apps, it focuses on the ones you want to run as fast as possible. And it will have some really cool features.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hopefully, things will get better soon. :)&lt;/p&gt;
</content>
        
