&lt;span class=&quot;giallo-l&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #9399B2;&quot;&gt;          &amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #89B4FA;&quot;&gt;cmd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #9399B2;&quot;&gt;&amp;quot;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #A6E3A1;&quot;&gt; &amp;quot;$TERMINAL start broot&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #9399B2;&quot;&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;giallo-l&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #9399B2;&quot;&gt;          &amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #89B4FA;&quot;&gt;shortcut&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #9399B2;&quot;&gt;&amp;quot;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #A6E3A1;&quot;&gt; &amp;quot;b&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;giallo-l&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #9399B2;&quot;&gt;        }&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;giallo-l&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #9399B2;&quot;&gt;      ]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;giallo-l&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #9399B2;&quot;&gt;    }&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;giallo-l&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #9399B2;&quot;&gt;  ]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;giallo-l&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #9399B2;&quot;&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lot of interesting things here!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Groups have different colors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No group names&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Setting font size, button size, and buttons per row can be set&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;And most interesting is support for shell magic variables, like (&lt;code&gt;$HOME&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;$TERMINAL&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;~&lt;/code&gt;, etc.)!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So now the program will launch using the preferred terminal, use the default file manager to open the folders, etc&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Awesome!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And no more checking configuration files every 2 seconds, because the program exits after launching.
It is now a run, and bye program, instead of staying in memory doing nothing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Forgot what else I want to do in this, but I will get back to it,
after I have made progress on my other pet project.&lt;/p&gt;
</content>
        
